## Build and preview

```sh
python3 scripts/build-site.py            # writes _site/ (git-ignored)
mkdir -p /tmp/p && ln -sfn "$PWD/_site" /tmp/p/xynovim && python3 -m http.server -d /tmp/p 8000
# open http://localhost:8000/xynovim/   (the /xynovim/ prefix is how Pages serves it)
```

The numbers on the page come from the README (tests badge, test summary) and from `tests/*_spec.lua`, so they cannot drift; the spec `tests/site_spec.lua` checks the built site (links, assets, CSP, alt texts, budgets, the workflow).
'''),
    ...text(r'Three commands. The build writes _site/, which git ignores (a test checks that). To preview, the site is symlinked into a temporary directory under the name xynovim and served by Python’s http.server, because the real site lives under a path prefix: the README says the /xynovim/ prefix is how Pages serves it, and the 404 page uses absolute /xynovim/ paths. The comment in the second block is the whole instruction: open localhost:8000/xynovim/.'),
